# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Convert to QUBO format {#convert-to-qubo-format}"
msgstr "Convertir al formato QUBO {#convert-to-qubo-format}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now transform the constrained optimization problem into QUBO format:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora transformamos el problema de optimización con restricciones al formato"
" QUBO:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Convert QUBO to Iskay format {#convert-qubo-to-iskay-format}"
msgstr "Convertir QUBO al formato de Iskay {#convert-qubo-to-iskay-format}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we need to convert the QUBO object into the dictionary format required "
"by Kipu Quantum's Iskay Optimizer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora necesitamos convertir el objeto QUBO al formato de diccionario "
"requerido por el Iskay Optimizer de Kipu Quantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `problem` and `problem_type` arguments encode an optimization problem of"
" the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Los argumentos `problem` y `problem_type` codifican un problema de "
"optimización de la forma\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"\\min_{(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\in D} C(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
"where\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"\\min_{(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\in D} C(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
"donde\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C(x_1, ... , x_n) = a + \\sum_{i} b_i x_i + \\sum_{i, j} c_{i, j} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum_{k_1, ..., k_m} g_{k_1, ..., k_m} x_{k_1} ... x_{k_m}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C(x_1, ... , x_n) = a + \\sum_{i} b_i x_i + \\sum_{i, j} c_{i, j} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum_{k_1, ..., k_m} g_{k_1, ..., k_m} x_{k_1} ... x_{k_m}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By choosing `problem_type = \"binary\"`, you specify that the cost function "
"is in `binary` format, which means that $D = \\{0,  1\\}^{n}$, as in, the "
"cost function is written in QUBO/HUBO formulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Al elegir `problem_type = \"binary\"`, especificas que la función de costo "
"está en formato `binary`, lo que significa que $D = \\{0,  1\\}^{n}$, es "
"decir, la función de costo está escrita en formulación QUBO/HUBO.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, by choosing `problem_type = \"spin\"`, the cost function "
"is written in Ising formulation, where $D = \\{-1, 1\\}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por otro lado, al elegir `problem_type = \"spin\"`, la función de costo está"
" escrita en formulación de Ising, donde $D = \\{-1, 1\\}^{n}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The coefficients of the problem should be encoded in a dictionary as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align} \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\{} \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"()\"}&: \\quad &a, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i,)\"}&: \\quad &b_i, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i, j)\"}&: \\quad &c_{i, j}, \\quad (i \\neq j) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\quad  \\vdots \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(} k_1, ..., k_m  \\texttt{)\"}&: \\quad &g_{k_1, ..., k_m}, \\quad (k_1 \\neq k_2 \\neq \\dots \\neq k_m) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\}}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Los coeficientes del problema deben codificarse en un diccionario de la siguiente manera:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align} \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\{} \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"()\"}&: \\quad &a, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i,)\"}&: \\quad &b_i, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i, j)\"}&: \\quad &c_{i, j}, \\quad (i \\neq j) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\quad  \\vdots \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(} k_1, ..., k_m  \\texttt{)\"}&: \\quad &g_{k_1, ..., k_m}, \\quad (k_1 \\neq k_2 \\neq \\dots \\neq k_m) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\}}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the keys of the dictionary must be strings containing a valid "
"tuple of non-repeating integers. For binary problems, we know that:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ten en cuenta que las claves del diccionario deben ser cadenas que contengan"
" una tupla válida de enteros no repetidos. Para problemas binarios, sabemos "
"que:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x_i^2 = x_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x_i^2 = x_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $i=j$ (since $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ means $x_i \\cdot x_i = x_i$). So, in "
"your QUBO formulation, if you have both linear contributions $b_i x_i$ and "
"diagonal quadratic contributions $c_{i,i} x_i^2$, these terms must be "
"combined into a single linear coefficient:\n"
msgstr ""
"para $i=j$ (ya que $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ implica $x_i \\cdot x_i = x_i$). "
"Entonces, en su formulación QUBO, si tiene tanto contribuciones lineales "
"$b_i x_i$ como contribuciones cuadráticas diagonales $c_{i,i} x_i^2$, estos "
"términos deben combinarse en un único coeficiente lineal:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Total linear coefficient for variable $x_i$:** $b_i + c_{i,i}$\n"
msgstr "**Coeficiente lineal total para la variable $x_i$:** $b_i + c_{i,i}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means:\n"
"- Linear terms like `\"(i, )\"` contain: original linear coefficient + diagonal quadratic coefficient\n"
"- Diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, i)\"` should **NOT** appear in the final dictionary\n"
"- Only off-diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, j)\"` where $i \\neq j$ should be included as separate entries\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto significa:\n"
"- Los términos lineales como `\"(i, )\"` contienen: coeficiente lineal original + coeficiente cuadrático diagonal\n"
"- Los términos cuadráticos diagonales como `\"(i, i)\"` **NO** deben aparecer en el diccionario final\n"
"- Solo los términos cuadráticos fuera de la diagonal como `\"(i, j)\"` donde $i \\neq j$ deben incluirse como entradas separadas\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example:** If your QUBO has $3x_1 + 2x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2$, the Iskay dictionary should contain:\n"
"- `\"(0, )\"`: `5.0` (combining $3 + 2 = 5$)\n"
"- `\"(0, 1)\"`: `4.0` (off-diagonal term)\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ejemplo:** Si su QUBO tiene $3x_1 + 2x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2$, el diccionario de Iskay debe contener:\n"
"- `\"(0, )\"`: `5.0` (combinando $3 + 2 = 5$)\n"
"- `\"(0, 1)\"`: `4.0` (término fuera de la diagonal)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**NOT** separate entries for `\"(0, )\"`: `3.0` and `\"(0, 0)\"`: `2.0`.\n"
msgstr "**NO** entradas separadas para `\"(0, )\"`: `3.0` y `\"(0, 0)\"`: `2.0`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the bf-DCQO algorithm {#understand-the-bf-dcqo-algorithm}"
msgstr "Comprender el algoritmo bf-DCQO {#understand-the-bf-dcqo-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we run the optimization, let's understand the sophisticated quantum "
"algorithm that powers Iskay: **bf-DCQO (bias-field digitized counterdiabatic"
" quantum optimization)** [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Antes de ejecutar la optimización, comprendamos el sofisticado algoritmo "
"cuántico que impulsa a Iskay: **bf-DCQO (bias-field digitized "
"counterdiabatic quantum optimization)** [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is bf-DCQO? {#what-is-bf-dcqo}"
msgstr "¿Qué es bf-DCQO? {#what-is-bf-dcqo}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"bf-DCQO is based on the time evolution of a quantum system where the problem"
" solution is encoded in the **ground state** (lowest energy state) of the "
"final quantum Hamiltonian [\\[1\\]](#references). The algorithm addresses a "
"fundamental challenge in quantum optimization:\n"
msgstr ""
"bf-DCQO se basa en la evolución temporal de un sistema cuántico donde la "
"solución del problema está codificada en el **estado fundamental** (estado "
"de menor energía) del Hamiltoniano cuántico final [\\[1\\]](#references). El"
" algoritmo aborda un desafío fundamental en la optimización cuántica:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The challenge**: Traditional adiabatic quantum computing requires very "
"slow evolution to maintain ground state conditions according to the "
"adiabatic theorem. This demands increasingly deep quantum circuits as "
"problem complexity grows, leading to more gate operations and accumulated "
"errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"**El desafío**: La computación cuántica adiabática tradicional requiere una "
"evolución muy lenta para mantener las condiciones del estado fundamental "
"según el teorema adiabático. Esto exige circuitos cuánticos cada vez más "
"profundos a medida que crece la complejidad del problema, lo que conduce a "
"más operaciones de compuertas y errores acumulados.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The solution**: bf-DCQO uses counterdiabatic protocols to enable rapid "
"evolution while maintaining ground state fidelity, dramatically reducing "
"circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"**La solución**: bf-DCQO utiliza protocolos contradiabáticos para permitir "
"una evolución rápida mientras mantiene la fidelidad del estado fundamental, "
"reduciendo drásticamente la profundidad de los circuitos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical framework {#mathematical-framework}"
msgstr "Marco matemático {#mathematical-framework}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The algorithm minimizes a cost function of the form:\n"
msgstr "El algoritmo minimiza una función de costo de la forma:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\min_{(x_1,x_2,...,x_n) \\in D} C(x_1,x_2,...,x_n)$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\min_{(x_1,x_2,...,x_n) \\in D} C(x_1,x_2,...,x_n)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where $D = \\{0,1\\}^n$ for binary variables and:\n"
msgstr "donde $D = \\{0,1\\}^n$ para variables binarias y:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$C(x) = a + \\sum_i b_i x_i + \\sum_{i,j} c_{ij} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum "
"g_{k_1,...,k_m} x_{k_1}...x_{k_m}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$C(x) = a + \\sum_i b_i x_i + \\sum_{i,j} c_{ij} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum "
"g_{k_1,...,k_m} x_{k_1}...x_{k_m}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For our Market Split problem, the cost function is:\n"
msgstr "Para nuestro problema de Market Split, la función de costo es:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$C(x) = ||Ax - b||^2 = x^T A^T A x - 2 b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"
msgstr "$$C(x) = ||Ax - b||^2 = x^T A^T A x - 2 b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The role of counterdiabatic terms {#the-role-of-counterdiabatic-terms}"
msgstr ""
"El papel de los términos contradiabáticos {#the-role-of-counterdiabatic-"
"terms}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Counterdiabatic terms** are additional terms introduced into the time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian that suppress unwanted excitations during the quantum "
"evolution. Here's why they're crucial:\n"
msgstr ""
"Los **términos contradiabáticos** son términos adicionales introducidos en "
"el Hamiltoniano dependiente del tiempo que suprimen las excitaciones no "
"deseadas durante la evolución cuántica. A continuación se explica por qué "
"son cruciales:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In adiabatic quantum optimization, we evolve the system according to a time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian:\n"
msgstr ""
"En la optimización cuántica adiabática, evolucionamos el sistema de acuerdo "
"con un Hamiltoniano dependiente del tiempo:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$H(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{T}\\right) H_{\\text{initial}} + \\frac{t}{T} "
"H_{\\text{problem}}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$H(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{T}\\right) H_{\\text{initial}} + \\frac{t}{T} "
"H_{\\text{problem}}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H_{\\text{problem}}$ encodes our optimization problem. To maintain "
"the ground state during rapid evolution, we add counterdiabatic terms:\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $H_{\\text{problem}}$ codifica nuestro problema de optimización. Para "
"mantener el estado fundamental durante una evolución rápida, añadimos "
"términos contradiabáticos:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$H_{\\text{CD}}(t) = H(t) + H_{\\text{counter}}(t)$$\n"
msgstr "$$H_{\\text{CD}}(t) = H(t) + H_{\\text{counter}}(t)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These counterdiabatic terms do the following:\n"
"1. **Suppress unwanted transitions**: Prevent the quantum state from jumping to excited states during fast evolution\n"
"2. **Enable shorter evolution times**: Allow us to reach the final state much faster without violating adiabaticity\n"
"3. **Reduce circuit depth**: Shorter evolution leads to fewer gates and less error\n"
msgstr ""
"Estos términos contradiabáticos hacen lo siguiente:\n"
"1. **Suprimen transiciones no deseadas**: Evitan que el estado cuántico salte a estados excitados durante una evolución rápida\n"
"2. **Permiten tiempos de evolución más cortos**: Nos permiten alcanzar el estado final mucho más rápido sin violar la adiabaticidad\n"
"3. **Reducen la profundidad del circuito**: Una evolución más corta conduce a menos compuertas y menos errores\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The practical impact is dramatic: bf-DCQO uses up to **10 times fewer "
"entangling gates** than Digital Quantum Annealing [\\[1\\]](#references), "
"making it practical for today's noisy quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"El impacto práctico es dramático: bf-DCQO utiliza hasta **10 veces menos "
"compuertas de entrelazamiento** que el Digital Quantum Annealing "
"[\\[1\\]](#references), lo que lo hace práctico para el hardware cuántico "
"ruidoso de la actualidad.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bias-field iterative optimization {#bias-field-iterative-optimization}"
msgstr ""
"Optimización iterativa con campo de sesgo {#bias-field-iterative-"
"optimization}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike variational algorithms that optimize circuit parameters through many "
"iterations, bf-DCQO uses a **bias-field guided approach** that converges in "
"approximately 10 iterations [1]:\n"
msgstr ""
"A diferencia de los algoritmos variacionales que optimizan los parámetros "
"del circuito a través de muchas iteraciones, bf-DCQO utiliza un **enfoque "
"guiado por campo de sesgo** que converge en aproximadamente 10 iteraciones "
"[1]:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Iteration process:**\n"
msgstr "**Proceso de iteración:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Initial quantum evolution**: Start with a quantum circuit implementing the"
" counterdiabatic evolution protocol\n"
msgstr ""
"**Evolución cuántica inicial**: Comenzar con un circuito cuántico que "
"implementa el protocolo de evolución contradiabática\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Measurement**: Measure the quantum state to obtain a probability "
"distribution over bitstrings\n"
msgstr ""
"**Medición**: Medir el estado cuántico para obtener una distribución de "
"probabilidad sobre cadenas de bits\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Bias-field calculation**: Analyze the measurement statistics and calculate an optimal bias-field $h_i$ for each qubit:\n"
"$$h_i = \\text{f}(\\text{measurement statistics}, \\text{previous solutions})$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Cálculo del campo de sesgo**: Analizar las estadísticas de medición y calcular un campo de sesgo óptimo $h_i$ para cada qubit:\n"
"$$h_i = \\text{f}(\\text{measurement statistics}, \\text{previous solutions})$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Next iteration**: The bias-field modifies the Hamiltonian for the next iteration:\n"
"$$H_{\\text{next}} = H_{\\text{problem}} + \\sum_i h_i \\sigma_i^z$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Siguiente iteración**: El campo de sesgo modifica el Hamiltoniano para la siguiente iteración:\n"
"$$H_{\\text{next}} = H_{\\text{problem}} + \\sum_i h_i \\sigma_i^z$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This allows starting near the previously found good solution, effectively"
" performing a form of \"quantum local search\"\n"
msgstr ""
"   Esto permite comenzar cerca de la solución buena encontrada previamente, "
"realizando efectivamente una forma de \"búsqueda local cuántica\"\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Convergence**: Repeat until the solution quality stabilizes or a maximum "
"number of iterations is reached\n"
msgstr ""
"**Convergencia**: Repetir hasta que la calidad de la solución se estabilice "
"o se alcance un número máximo de iteraciones\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key advantage**: Each iteration provides meaningful progress toward the "
"optimal solution by incorporating information from previous measurements, "
"unlike variational methods that must explore the parameter space blindly.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ventaja clave**: Cada iteración proporciona un progreso significativo "
"hacia la solución óptima al incorporar información de mediciones anteriores,"
" a diferencia de los métodos variacionales que deben explorar el espacio de "
"parámetros a ciegas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Integrated classical post-processing {#integrated-classical-post-processing}"
msgstr ""
"Post-procesamiento clásico integrado {#integrated-classical-post-processing}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After the quantum optimization converges, Iskay performs classical **local "
